fraqtive (@VERSION@) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Build on Qt 6: the 3D view is one stereo area with two parallel cameras
    fitted to the depth limits of Stereo KWin (on Wayland; flat on X11, and
    the window says so), with the options Enable 3D and Render Resolution per
    Eye and a shortcut to Display Settings, its sentences in ten languages.
  * Build-Depends: Qt 6 (qt6-base-dev, qt6-base-private-dev, qt6-l10n-tools,
    libqt6opengl6-dev, libqt6openglwidgets6), libstereo-declare-dev, libx11-dev.
  * The camera separation is the person's depth limits for the screen, never
    scaled by the size of the window or of the 3D view (ORDER 750): the limits
    come in the pixels of the view's buffer from libstereo-declare 1.11
    (limit * output width / 1920 * buffer width / shown width), so the same
    scene has the same separation on the output in a small window, full screen
    and at 50 % render resolution. Build-Depends and Depends: libstereo-declare 1.11.
